Subject: [PATCH] vayu: test26 IPA data path - 0029 post-auth/SRAM/ttbrfix, 0041 QMI stages, GSI 4.1 channels + QMAP + en1

Base: vayu-test26 d15caf0 (/mnt/ramdisk/n13c/src). Applies with -p1.
Kernel: mach-data1.bin sha256 271855dc69e96b48cc31fa2b56f6c37da0b9a224abc3554e817886664cdc041b.

What:
- 0029 (ported by hand to this tree): vayu_ipa_bus mask, vayu_ipa_post_auth_ms with read-only
  GSI/uC look, vayu_ipa_sram=1 canaries at 0x1e47000, vayu_ipa_ttbrfix, and the 4-page SMMU
  identity map for the whole 2 GiB DDR window. vayu_pas already had the opt-in forced shutdown
  (vayu_ipa_pas bit 0), so that part of 0029 is not duplicated.
- 0041 (ported with the hakios.qmi/hakios.qrtr names of this tree): vayu_ipa_qmi=0..4 stages,
  one INIT_MODEM_DRIVER, INDICATION_REGISTER, INIT_COMPLETE_IND from the published 0x31/1 port,
  read-only WDS Get Packet Service Status at stage 3, WDS Start allowed only at stage 4.
- New data files from the net1 line: vayu_ipa_data.c (GSI 2.0 ch4/EP5 cmd, ch5/EP10 LAN,
  ch3/EP2 WAN TX, ch6/EP11 WAN RX; endpoints, empty filter/route/header/proc tables, SRAM
  readback, polling thread, QMAP encode/decode), vayu_cell_net.c (en1, IFNET_FAMILY_CELLULAR,
  IFT_CELLULAR, raw IPv4, SIOCPROTOATTACH + SIOCAIFADDR + IFF_UP/RUNNING, optional default route)
  and vayu_cell_qmap.h. vayu_ipa_data_prepare() runs before MPSS after ipa_fws; WDS Start is
  refused unless the IPA QMI handshake, all four GSI channels/tables and en1 are ready.
- vayu_cell_data.c wires WDS Start (APN: vayu_cell_apn, default SIM profile; IPv4), WDS Get
  Current Settings (address/gateway/mask/DNS/MTU) into vayu_cell_net_session().
- One index line per stage, greppable:
    vayu-data: S1 IPA QMI READY / S2 GSI CHANNELS / S3 DPM OPEN PORT / S4 WDA SET DATA FORMAT /
    S5 WDS BIND MUX / S6 WDS IP FAMILY / S7 WDS START / S8 WDS GET SETTINGS /
    S9 EN1 IFNET / S10 FIRST PACKET   -> OK|ERROR|TIMEOUT ...

Boot-args: vayu_ipa=1 vayu_ipa_data=1 vayu_ipa_qmi=4 vayu_cell_data=1 vayu_cell_net=1
  (+ vayu_ipa_ttbrfix=1 vayu_ipa_bus=6 vayu_ipa_post_auth_ms=8000 vayu_ipa_sram=1,
   vayu_cell_net_default=1 only if a default route is wanted).

Known limits (fail closed, no claim): no CommCenter/configd and no DNS publication (en1 only,
kern.vayu.cellular_* for the settings); the modem's runtime filter installation is not implemented,
so an INSTALL_FILTER_RULE request clears data_ready and blocks Start; uC NOT READY after AUTH is
still only observed, stock ipa3_post_init's command pipe is approximated by the four channels and
the immediate table commands. vayu_ipa_sram=1 moves the SRAM window to 0x1e47000, and both the
canary writes and the table readback use that same window (vayu_ipa_sram_base()).

